From: Emception maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] sysconfig: honor cross project base on Windows

The Emscripten cross-build sets _PYTHON_PROJECT_BASE to the target build
directory. A Windows host otherwise looks for pyconfig.h beside the native
bootstrap interpreter, which makes generate-posix-vars fail before the target
build starts.

Keep CPython's native Windows behavior unless the cross-build explicitly
provides _PYTHON_PROJECT_BASE.
---
 Lib/sysconfig/__init__.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Lib/sysconfig/__init__.py b/Lib/sysconfig/__init__.py
--- a/Lib/sysconfig/__init__.py
+++ b/Lib/sysconfig/__init__.py
@@ -429 +429 @@
-        if os.name == "nt":
+        if os.name == "nt" and "_PYTHON_PROJECT_BASE" not in os.environ:
